# Even orthogonal covering reductions

The odd orthogonal row, minus rank two and minus rank three over q > 2 lift
through actual symplectic, linear and unitary carrier comparisons. Their
independent family-lifting premises remain explicit for the parent assembly.

The higher plus and minus rows have consumers of the precise universal
two-kernel calculation. Those bounds, the plus rank-three comparison, and
the binary minus rank-three comparison are not established by this module.
In particular, D₄(2) must retain its exceptional two-primary multiplier.

Source: Aschbacher–Smith B.1.13, printed pp.73–74; GLS3 §§2.7 and 6.1.
-/
